Spec: Ride tracking

Purpose:
  Records a ride: the process-lifetime @RideTracker, the GPS fix filter and route recorder,
    location source and permission gate, the Android foreground service, the iOS Live Activity,
    platform control relay, battery-optimization hint and the countdown voice cue.

Owns:
  ./ride_tracker.dart
  ./ride_tracking_state.dart
  ./route_recorder.dart
  ./gps_fix_filter.dart
  ./gps_signal.dart
  ./location_fix.dart
  ./location_source.dart
  ./location_permission.dart
  ./geolocator_permission_service.dart
  ./permission_gate_dialog.dart
  ./ride_recording_controller.dart
  ./foreground_task_service.dart
  ./live_activity_service.dart
  ./ride_control_relay.dart
  ./ride_notification.dart
  ./battery_optimization.dart
  ./countdown_announcer.dart
  ./tracking_providers.dart
  /test/tracking

References:
  /docs/specs/history/05-gps-tracking.md
  /docs/specs/history/05b-gps-platform.md
  /docs/specs/history/06-live-activity.md
  /docs/specs/history/21-countdown-cue.md
  /ios/ios.sdd
  /android/android.sdd

Exposes:
  @RideTracker state: location, track points, distance, speed, elapsed time, paused flag, activity type

Must:
  @RideTracker is a process-lifetime singleton that survives screen disposal and works fully offline.
  @RideTracker owns the ride lifecycle and persistence; @RouteRecorder builds the route from accepted fixes.
  Tracking and the location stream run in the main isolate; the foreground service only keeps the process
    alive, shows the notification and relays its buttons.
  Every fix updates the live location and speed, even while paused.
  A fix is recorded only when it is fresh (at most `5` s old by its capture time), accurate to `35` m,
    not stationary (provider speed below `0.8` m/s), not an outlier (above `50` m/s), moved at least
    the larger of `8` m and both accuracies, and implies at least `0.5` m/s over at most `60` s.
  More than `60` s after the last recorded point, a fix is held until a rolling run or a fix `10` s later
    confirms real progress; confirmed held fixes are replayed in order, unconfirmed ones are dropped on
    start, resume and stop.
  Resume does not count the paused gap as distance.
  A trackpoint is timestamped with when the fix was taken.
  Fix age and elapsed time come from the platform capture timestamp, never from ingestion time.
  The ride starts only after the permission gate grants location; Android 13+ also asks for notifications,
    iOS escalates to Always for screen-off recording.
  Pause, resume, stop and open mean the same from the notification, the Live Activity and the app,
    through @rideControlRelay.
  Swiping the app away finalizes the active ride with an end time.
  The countdown cue never throws into the countdown and never delays a tick; it is silent on Android
    when the ringer is not normal.

Must not:
  Move recording logic into the foreground-task isolate.
  Request the `REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS` permission.

Done when:
  The ported @RideTracker tests and `/test/tracking/stop_recovery_scenarios_test.dart` pass.
  Recording with the screen off, notification controls and offline recording are checked on a device.
